  "summary": "A good Vastu assessment begins with **accurate description, clear scope and transparent reasoning.** You do not begin with remedies; you begin with what the property actually contains.",
  "takeHome": "**Take-home task (ungraded, 10 min):** Draw a rough sketch of your own home or a friend's (with permission). Mark the entrance and list five things you can *observe* without interpreting.",
  "checklist": [
    "Write the **scope line**: \"This assessment covers ___ and does not cover ___.\"",
    "Identify the **property type** and what it lets you observe.",
    "Name the **framework or school** you are applying (or write \"to be confirmed\").",
    "Check the plan for a **north marker, dimensions and clear labels**; if any is missing, ask, do not assume.",
    "Write \"**approximate**\" next to any unverified measurement.",
    "Never treat the **top of the page as north**.",
    "Mark the plot boundary, entrance, secondary doors, rooms, open areas and circulation.",
    "Record **at least three observations as facts only** (no good/bad/lucky/defective).",
    "Write interpretations that name the guideline, its certainty, and whether schools differ.",
    "Write recommendations that are **feasible, prioritised and verified by the right professional**.",
    "Put **safety, ventilation, drainage and structure first** in every report.",
    "Document deviations from a preference as **differences, not defects**.",
    "Compare the drawing with the **present building** (extensions, conversions, alterations).",
    "Remove any wording that **promises health, wealth, relationship or career outcomes**.",
    "Remember: \"**Not knowing is a valid finding. State it and verify it.**\""
  ],
