      "answer": "*What a good answer contains:* \"N\" written at the corner/edge nearest the arrow; labels running clockwise N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W, NW; opposite cells correct (N/S, E/W, NE/SW, NW/SE); a remark that, because the arrow points to a corner, the cardinal directions fall near the corners of the rectangle and the diagonals near its sides. A note that the result is provisional until the arrow's source is known."
