    "summary":  "A respectful prayer-space assessment **balances traditional preferences with the family\u0027s practices, the available layout and safe use.** A dedicated room is not mandatory; a stable, clean, well-ventilated niche or cabinet can serve. Record limitations, offer feasible alternatives, and never move sacred objects without consent.",
    "takeHome":  "**Take-home task (ungraded, 10 min):** In a home you know (with permission, or a hypothetical one), identify a quiet corner. List five *observable* features (position, light, ventilation, nearby combustibles, circulation) and one safety question. Do not interpret yet.",
    "checklist":  [
                      "Ask about the household\u0027s practice and customs before assessing anything.",
                      "Do not assume a dedicated prayer room is needed; niche, cabinet or corner can serve.",
                      "Obtain consent before touching, moving or photographing sacred objects.",
                      "Verify the plan\u0027s orientation (source of north) before stating any direction.",
                      "Record whether you mean idol facing or worshipper facing, and what the family says.",
                      "Name the framework; state the commonly taught preference (North-East, with East or North as variations) as a tradition, not a rule.",
                      "Check flame: stable base, non-combustible surface, clearance from fabrics, garlands and paper.",
                      "Check incense: holder with ash catcher, ventilation, smoke-sensitive occupants.",
                      "Check electrical: sockets, extension boards, fairy lights; refer doubtful wiring to a qualified electrician.",
                      "Check shelf or platform: level, fixed, strong enough; refer cracks or looseness to a qualified professional.",
                      "Confirm the prayer space does not block a door or escape route; store matches and oils out of children\u0027s reach.",
                      "Check access for elders and people with limited mobility, and note circulation.",
                      "If the preferred location is unavailable, document the limitation and offer a low-disruption alternative; no construction by default.",
                      "Write F/I/R, tag each recommendation by priority, note consent, and promise no outcomes."
                  ],
