    "extraPractice":  [
                          {
                              "id":  "d11-ep-1",
                              "task":  "**Exercise 1 - Rewrite the judgement.** Rewrite this note as three separate F, I and R lines: *\"The pantry is in a bad place and the staircase is wrong, so the family will lose money.\"*",
                              "answer":  "F lines are neutral facts with verified direction (\"The pantry is in the north-east portion; the stair rises counter-clockwise\"). The I line names the Framework Reference rows and says schools differ. The R line begins with practical checks (dryness, pests, handrails, lighting) and offers low-disruption options. No word like bad or wrong and no financial prediction. Model: **F:** \"The pantry is in the north-east portion; the stair is in the south-east portion and rises counter-clockwise (north verified).\" **I:** \"Commonly taught guidance prefers the south-west or north-west for a pantry and the south, south-west or west for a stair with clockwise ascent; schools differ, and no outcome is implied.\" **R:** \"Priority 1: check the pantry for dryness and pests; check the stair\u0027s handrail, lighting and treads. Priority 2: record the deviations; no structural change is suggested.\""
                          },
                          {
                              "id":  "d11-ep-2",
                              "task":  "**Exercise 2 - Plan the safe-first conversation.** Prepare three questions you would ask a household about a safe, in a polite order, and one thing you would never ask.",
                              "answer":  "Questions on anchoring/fixing, visibility and who knows the access code or key; also on insurance and off-site copies. The \"never\" item is a request to see the contents or be told the combination. A strong answer starts with a neutral opening (\"May I note how the safe is fixed?\") and does not suggest a direction until security has been recorded."
                          },
                          {
                              "id":  "d11-ep-3",
                              "task":  "**Exercise 3 - Build a services map.** Draw a simple sketch of your home (or a hypothetical one) showing the electrical panel, water valve, gas shut-off, staircase and one store. Mark whether each is reachable without moving anything. Write two recommendations and one referral.",
                              "answer":  "Clear symbols from the legend; a verified or \"unknown\" north; honest ticks (not all green); recommendations that clear access or fix visible hazards; a referral to the right professional (electrician for the panel, plumber for a valve). No directional claims unless north is verified."
                          }
                      ],
