    "summary":  "A complete assessment includes secondary spaces and distinguishes **traditional recommendations** from **real security, access, fire and structural requirements.** Storage, safes, pantries and stairs are judged first by access, dryness, stability and protection; direction is recorded as an interpretation, and deviation is documented rather than called a defect.",
    "takeHome":  "**Take-home task (ungraded, 10 min):** Walk through your own home (or a hypothetical plan) and list the electrical panel, water and gas shut-offs, and the staircase. For each, write one observation about whether it is clear and reachable. Do not interpret yet.",
    "checklist":  [
                      "Verify north first; note the source. If it is unknown, write \"unknown\" and do not state directions.",
                      "Locate the electrical panel, meter, water valve and gas shut-off before looking at anything else.",
                      "Check that every service is reachable without moving stored goods.",
                      "Check doors, windows and vents are not blocked by storage.",
                      "Look for damp, seepage, fungus and pests before commenting on direction.",
                      "Check stacking height, shelf strength and the position of heavy and flammable items.",
                      "Safe: anchored? hidden? fire protection? who knows the code or key? insured? load checked?",
                      "Record the safe\u0027s direction only after the security points; never imply financial results.",
                      "Pantry: sealed containers, dry, away from heat, rotated stock, no pests.",
                      "Staircase: headroom, handrail, lighting, even treads, slip resistance, clear landings, guards.",
                      "Under-stair space: no flammables, no blocked panels, no cramped sealed cupboard.",
                      "Auxiliary spaces: privacy, ventilation, access, drainage, electrical safety, dignified conditions.",
                      "Write F, I and R separately; no words like good, bad, lucky, defective in the F column.",
                      "Compare with the Framework Reference only after practical checks; say \"schools differ\".",
                      "Refer structural, electrical, plumbing, gas, fire and security matters to qualified professionals; never recommend moving or altering a stair."
                  ],
