                              "id":  "d13-ep-1",
                              "task":  "**Exercise 1 — Rewrite the opinion as an observation.**\n*What to do:* Rewrite these as neutral observed conditions: (a) \"The bedroom is cramped and badly lit.\" (b) \"The kitchen is in a bad place.\" (c) \"The wall is dangerous.\"",
                              "answer":  "*What a good answer contains:* Measurable or photographable statements and a source. For example: (a) \"Bedroom measures about 9 ft x 10 ft (taped today); one window, closed during the visit; no lux reading taken.\" (b) \"Kitchen door at the far end of the plan; orientation unverified, so no directional statement.\" (c) \"Vertical crack about 60 cm long in the wall near the staircase, photographed today.\" The word \"dangerous\" is replaced with an observation and a referral to a structural professional."
